          "id": "87b8e1f5eeddd6e7053d11ce4d448bd581dd1ddc",
          "message": "test(sparq-fedplan-mpc): correctness coverage (sq-bif) [OPUS-4.8] (#1232)\n\nAdd 10 mutation-verified correctness tests to the EXISTING test modules of\nsparq-fedplan-mpc (no new feature/cfg-gate), closing genuine behavioural and\nsoundness-invariant gaps the prior suite left untested. All assert specific\nbehaviour, not \"no panic\"/tautology.\n\nselection.rs:\n- total_cardinality sums ONLY surviving candidates (== upstream total minus the\n  pruned source's estimate; strictly lower) — a regression that summed pruned\n  candidates is caught.\n- participating_sources deduplicates a source contributing to MULTIPLE patterns\n  (verified by a mutation that removed the dedup).\n- PruneReason::label pins the load-bearing `participates=false` diagnostic token.\n\nenvelope.rs (the MPC soundness boundary):\n- An empty-predicate GlobalIri operand is honestly recorded as the `<global-iri>`\n  placeholder when disclosed (not dropped, not a panic).\n- C-B fail-closed invariant: a `<global-iri>` placeholder is disclosed BY\n  CONVENTION, so a deny-all holder must NOT spuriously reject it (verified by a\n  mutation that removed the skip — 2 tests fail without it).\n- The holder-exempt / verifier-counted asymmetry: the placeholder is skipped by\n  the holder C-B check yet still counts against the verifier budget (budget 0\n  rejects, budget 1 ratifies).\n- Cross-phase interaction: a private holder PRUNED at Phase 2 (non-participating)\n  no longer gates disclosability at Phase 3, so a predicate the remaining sources\n  mark public becomes Disclosed and the envelope records it — over the REAL\n  selection -> routing -> envelope path.\n\ncombination.rs:\n- A 5-pattern shared-variable chain collapses to one connected component.\n- Per-component `satisfiable` is independent of the global `bgp_satisfiable`\n  verdict (a live component reports true while an empty one reports false).\n- CombinationPruneReason::label names the witness pattern.\n\nCoverage (feature ON): line 98.46% -> 99.29%, region 98.59% -> 99.26%, missed\nfunctions 2 -> 0. The remaining uncovered lines are a deliberately-unreachable\ndefensive out-of-range guard, union-find path-halving (internal optimisation),\nand test-internal panic arms — not untested behaviour; no padding to hit them.\n\nGates green in BOTH feature states (default OFF + `fedplan-mpc` ON): build,\n`clippy --all-targets -D warnings`, test; rustfmt --check clean; rustdoc\nall-features (RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings) clean; typos clean. No public API change\n(test-only), so README/SKILL unchanged. All claims research-grade and NOT\nexternally audited (sq-qhy4 / sq-9hrn pending).\n\nAdvances sq-bif (not closed).\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-23T09:40:15Z",
