          "distinct": true,
          "id": "30db68e7534e1eefe48ecf98ae54c5628464516a",
          "message": "test(sparq-vectors): correctness coverage (sq-bif) [OPUS-4.8] (#1242)\n\nAdvances the workspace correctness-test sweep (P1 umbrella sq-bif) for\nsparq-vectors. The crate was already exceptionally well-covered, so this\ntargets the GENUINE remaining gaps in EXISTING test targets / EXISTING\nfeatures (NO new cargo feature or cfg-gate). All additions are test-only\n(+308 lines, 0 deletions); no public API, README, or SKILL change.\n\ndelta.rs (`delta` feature) — the `.spqd` decoder's fail-closed corruption\narms that the inline module's own header comment CLAIMED to cover but no\ntest actually exercised:\n  - an id in BOTH the append and tombstone sections (corrupt — the\n    load-bearing \"at most one of appended/tombstoned\" invariant);\n  - a non-finite (NaN / +inf) appended vector component;\n  - a duplicate id within the append section, and within the tombstone\n    section;\n  - a zero `dim` header; a trailing-garbage (longer-than-declared) file\n    rejected as a length mismatch.\nEach is forged from a valid sidecar so a dropped check would let a corrupt\n.spqd produce a silently-wrong store on replay.\n\nembed.rs (`provider` feature) — the `RemoteEmbedder::embed` response-\nvalidation contract (only the happy path + duplicate-index were tested):\nempty-input short-circuit (no request issued), transport-error\npropagation, non-JSON body, missing `data` array, wrong embedding count,\nwrong dimension, non-finite component, out-of-range index, missing index,\nand items missing `index`/`embedding`. Each is a fail-closed protocol-\nviolation a buggy/hostile provider could trigger.\n\nann.rs (default feature) — a focused unit gate for the `cosine` primitive\nthe exact searcher / filtered pre-filter / quantizers all rank with:\nknown orthogonal/opposite/45deg values, the zero-vector contract (a\ndefined 0.0, NEVER a NaN that would poison total_cmp sorting), a non-\nlane-multiple (dim 11 and dim 3) length so the SIMD tail loop is summed\nin, and the mismatched-dim panic.\n\nAssertions pin specific error messages / numeric values (not \"no panic\").\nCoverage (lib, delta+provider): ann.rs 87.3%->98.9%, delta.rs\n92.5%->96.1%, embed.rs 91.0%->94.6% lines. Gates green in BOTH feature\nstates: build/clippy --all-targets -D warnings/test default + delta,provider\n+ --all-features; workspace rustdoc --no-deps --all-features\nRUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings; rustfmt --check clean on the changed files (the\ndeferred-reformat diffs are only in untouched files). Umbrella sq-bif\nleft OPEN.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-23T12:11:00Z",
