          "committer": {
            "email": "noreply@github.com",
            "name": "GitHub",
            "username": "web-flow"
          },
          "distinct": true,
          "id": "98259ecdd66ff87683bca482fbc8ee786c4328a8",
          "message": "feat(vectors): cross-unit reconciliation in P4 grounding (sq-t80n4) [OPUS-4.8] (#1247)\n\nWire the landed P2 QUDT/SHACL unit-normalisation table (units.rs, sq-0wo9e.3)\ninto the P4 grounding render path so two quantities in DIFFERENT but COMMENSURABLE\nunits reconcile to a canonical SI unit before grounding / comparison / NL render,\ninstead of reading as distinct.\n\n- GroundingConfig::reconcile_units (default false — as-declared stays the default).\n- reconcile_quantity(TypedValue) -> TypedValue: the standalone primitive; threaded\n  through typed_values so both the TypedValue and NlString modalities honour it.\n- Conservative on unknown (load-bearing soundness): reconcile ONLY when\n  units::normalise resolves the unit; unknown / compound-rate units (e.g.\n  unit:KiloM-PER-HR = km/h, NOT in the simple-unit table) are left as declared,\n  never a fabricated factor. Only same-QuantityKind units reconcile.\n- Tests: mi<->km round-trip to canonical metres (tight epsilon), affine\n  degC<->K to kelvin, a NEGATIVE test that km/h stays as-declared, the\n  reconcile_quantity primitive's conservative contract, and the NL render path.\n\nNo new dependency, no new feature (same `structure` gate units.rs lives under; the\n`kge` CI leg already exercises the structure estate). No accuracy/perf claim — a\ncorrectness/grounding-ergonomics feature; any downstream payoff is empirical + EC2-gated.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-23T21:47:26Z",
          "tree_id": "3a8b27c41d131eaa1ca1a29d59ea01153e8610f7",
          "url": "https://github.com/jeswr/sparq/commit/98259ecdd66ff87683bca482fbc8ee786c4328a8"
